comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-28T20:43:45.137Z","harness:codex","Current recurrence on the complete 2,593-item corpus: the unfiltered all-lifecycle fuzzy sweep still refuses after exceeding its 1,000,000-pair safety limit, so this canonical scale issue remains accurate. An independent normalized exact-title census across all statuses found only the three already-canceled accidental probe items pm-11ag, pm-crpv, and pm-lql3. Bounded active plus canceled fuzzy review found those probes and distinct Semgrep finding records that intentionally retain separate finding identities; recent closed review found no new duplicate. This evidence does not substitute for the missing sub-quadratic full-corpus algorithm and therefore does not close the item."
  "2026-09-05T09:16:32.459Z","harness:codex","TDD evidence: baseline full-corpus duplicates fails with duplicate_sweep_cost_limit at 1,000,000 pairs on the complete 2,638-item corpus. Implementing exact prefix filtering with exhaustive reference mode and disclosed candidate/possible-pair costs. Property tests now preserve every qualifying exhaustive pair across thresholds, Unicode, empty tokens and issue identifiers."
  "2026-09-05T09:48:25.194Z","harness:codex","Token contract accounting: four additive cost fields disclose exact algorithm, total possible pairs, safety bound and recall guarantee. The duplicates JSON fixture increases from 94 to 124 estimated tokens; its ceiling is set to the measured 124 with no added slack. Existing help budget is preserved by shortening help wording. This is an explicit response-contract expansion, not an exemption from output gates."
  "2026-09-05T09:57:31.792Z","harness:codex","Scale evidence: the public metadata kernel scored 5k/50k/500k pairs at 10k/100k/1m items instead of 49,995,000/4,999,950,000/499,999,500,000 possible pairs. Exact-reference comparison and randomized scorer-oracle tests pass. Timings were 92/967/10108ms excluding filesystem ingestion. The one-second million-item acceptance target remains unmet and must not be recorded as complete."
  "2026-09-05T10:39:14.151Z","harness:codex","Installed-artifact acceptance: npm pack of this checkout installed independently with npm and Bun in disposable directories. Both completed 21 CLI operations including parent and children reads, exact duplicate parity, claim/update/comments/notes/learnings/files, linked public-SDK acceptance in explicit tracker sandbox context, structured close/release and clean history validation. Public SDK verified three complete items, duplicate analysis, 10000 candidate rows sampled to 256, final delivery validation and physical ledger ceiling. Local npx and bunx execute version 2026.9.5 in both installations. No real tracker was used by these tests."
  "2026-09-05T11:04:54.258Z","harness:codex","Final repeated benchmark preserves exact oracle recall and scores 5000/50000/500000 of 49995000/4999950000/499999500000 possible pairs at 10000/100000/1000000 items. Analysis times 92.05/864.06/10366.73ms exclude ingestion. The repeated million-item observation remains above the one-second tier; canonical remaining work is unchanged. Full quality:static passes."
  "2026-09-05T11:14:15.344Z","harness:codex","Delivery verification: full sandbox coverage passes 8442 tests in 613 files, exact 100/100/100/100 with zero uncovered (59977 lines, 62381 statements, 12941 functions, 47268 branches). Full quality:static, package-artifact and documentation-link gates pass. Every linked test on all six active owners passes through pm test --run --progress. npm and Bun installed-artifact acceptance passes 21 CLI operations each with public SDK assertions, npx and bunx. GitHub has no open issues, existing PRs or open dependency/code/secret security alerts; dependency audit is clean. Review and exact-head hosted checks remain the next delivery step."
notes[1]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-09-05T10:59:05.669Z","harness:codex","Delivery scope: the public in-memory exact prefix join and shared CLI/MCP path replace the all-token expansion, expose exhaustive oracle and exact-recall cost receipts, and make the live all-status duplicate check executable. The measured million-item batch is 10.108 seconds, so the broader one-second tier remains unfulfilled. Keep this canonical item open for incremental ingestion/analysis work after reviewed delivery; do not create a duplicate performance item."
